{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Arioch king of Ellasar.</b> From here is a hint to what the Sages said: the halakha follows Shmuel in civil laws and follows Rav in prohibitions. Arioch is Shmuel, and he is called Arioch because the halakha follows him in civil laws (דינין), for Arioch is an expression of kingship, as in לא ריכא ולא בר ריכא. And this is its meaning: אריוך מלך אל־סר — meaning אלא מאיסור — except for prohibitions, for the halakha follows Rav."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The comment is unvocalized and unpunctuated; the word division and reading of אל־סר / אלא מאיסור are inferred from context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:24.876994427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}